<div class="wrapper">
  <div class="sources-layer" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="panel">
      <header>
        <span class="eyebrow">GoogleFont · EmbedURL</span>
        <strong>Two roads into document.fonts</strong>
      </header>

      <div class="lanes">
        <div class="lane">
          <span class="lane-title">Google font by name</span>
          <ol>
            <li><code>fetch fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=…</code></li>
            <li>CSS into a detached <code>DOMParser</code> document — a bare <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> outside a document never parses its rules</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="lane">
          <span class="lane-title">Extract from a URL</span>
          <ol>
            <li><code>/api/font-proxy</code> fetches the page — <code>X-Frame-Options</code> pages can't be iframed</li>
            <li>Assemble a "manual iframe": <code>&lt;base href&gt;</code>, linked stylesheets, <code>@import</code>s, recursively</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tail">
        <span class="op">⇣</span>
        <div class="tail-box">
          <span class="lane-title">Shared tail</span>
          <p>
            Walk each sheet's <code>CSSFontFaceRule</code>s → absolutize + proxy the
            <code>src</code> URLs (webfont loads are CORS-gated) → <code>new FontFace(…).load()</code>
            → <code>document.fonts.add()</code> → dispatch <code>loadingdone</code>, and the dropdown
            already knows
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

